<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_user={@current_user}>
  <.chrome here="Policy"></.chrome>

  <div class="pbody legal-doc">
    <.section title="Who we are" pad>
      <p>
        cab is run by the NGO Debate Federation of Ukraine (ВМГО «Федерація Дебатів України»),
        the controller of the personal data described here.
        Address: <mark class="todo">[legal address]</mark>. ЄДРПОУ: <mark class="todo">[code]</mark>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Questions and requests about your data: <a href="mailto:support@uadebate.com">support@uadebate.com</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="mut">
        This policy follows the Law of Ukraine «Про захист персональних даних» (No. 2297-VI)
        and, for people in the European Union, the GDPR. cab is in beta testing; when we
        change this policy we update the date below and say so on this page.
        Last updated: 9 October 2026.
      </p>
    </.section>

    <.section title="What we store and why" pad>
      <p>
        <b>Your account.</b> When you sign in with GitHub we receive and keep your username,
        display name, e-mail address, avatar link and GitHub account number. We never see your
        password. We use these to sign you in and to show your name on rosters and draws.
        You can change your display name on your Account page.
      </p>
      <p>
        <b>Club membership.</b> When you ask to join a club we keep your request, the message
        and the contact you wrote for the club head, your role and the dates. The club head
        reads them to decide on your request.
      </p>
      <p>
        <b>Debates.</b> For each session you take part in we keep your registration, your seat
        in the draw, the motions, the ballots and scores, and the results. Standings and your
        personal statistics are computed from exactly these records.
      </p>
      <p>
        <b>Guests.</b> If you register without an account we keep the name you enter and a
        personal link to that one session. If a club head adds you by name, the same applies.
      </p>
      <p>
        <b>Invitations.</b> A club head can add a registered person by their exact username or
        e-mail. We keep the invitation until you accept or decline it.
      </p>
      <p>
        <b>Technical data.</b> Our web server logs each request (IP address, page, time and
        browser) to keep the service secure and working. These logs are kept for <mark class="todo">[retention, e.g. 14 days]</mark>.
      </p>
      <p class="mut">
        Legal basis: providing the service you asked for (GDPR Art. 6(1)(b); Law 2297-VI
        Art. 11), and our legitimate interest in running safe, fair debate sessions and keeping
        their results (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)).
      </p>
    </.section>

    <.section title="Cookies and browser storage" pad>
      <p>
        One cookie keeps you signed in. It is strictly necessary and needs no consent. Your
        theme choice (light, dark or system) is kept in your browser only and never sent to us.
        cab uses no analytics, no advertising and no third-party trackers, and its pages load
        nothing from other companies.
      </p>
    </.section>

    <.section title="Who else handles the data" pad>
      <p>
        <b>GitHub</b> handles your sign-in when you choose it. <b>Hetzner</b> hosts our servers
        in <mark class="todo">[data centre location]</mark>. We sell or give your data to no one.
      </p>
    </.section>

    <.section title="Who can see what" pad>
      <p>
        Club pages, session pages, draws and results are public, so anyone can see the names in
        them. A club can make its standings and roster visible to members only. Your account
        details, e-mail and join-request messages are never public.
      </p>
    </.section>

    <.section title="How long we keep it" pad>
      <p>
        Your account stays until you ask us to delete it. Results are the record of a debate
        and stay; when an account is deleted, its name in past results is replaced, so history
        stays complete without identifying you.
      </p>
      <p>
        Leaving a session before you are seated in a room, or being removed by the club head,
        deletes your name from it. A guest who leaves or is removed loses the guest account and
        the personal link. A guest who later signs in can move their results into their account,
        and the guest record is deleted.
      </p>
    </.section>

    <.section title="Your rights" pad>
      <p>
        You can ask to see your data, correct it, delete it, restrict or object to how we use
        it, and get a copy to take elsewhere. Write to
        <a href="mailto:support@uadebate.com">support@uadebate.com</a>
        and we answer within 30 days.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can also complain to the Ukrainian Parliament Commissioner for Human Rights
        (Уповноважений Верховної Ради України з прав людини) or, in the EU, to your data
        protection authority.
      </p>
    </.section>

    <.section title="Children" pad>
      <p>
        Many debaters are at school. If you are under 14, a parent or guardian should agree to
        your registration and can make any request on this page for you.
        <mark class="todo">[confirm the age with a lawyer]</mark>
      </p>
    </.section>
  </div>
</Layouts.app>
